strong>47\u00b0F</strong> was the 16th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 79 since 1948, the coolest since 2023. The normal high for the date is 54\u00b0F, and the record is 67\u00b0F (1964). The low of <strong>39\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Bridgeport has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Bridgeport's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Bridgeport has set <strong class=\"sig\">52 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 125 that chance alone would give, and <strong>158 record highs</strong>, more than the 125 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (59). Bridgeport's all-time high is 103\u00b0F, on July 22, 1957.","t_chg":"Bridgeport has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 77 complete years: Bridgeport's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.43\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.32 to +0.54), about +3.3\u00b0F since 1949. Bridgeport's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.29\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.16 to +0.42), about +2.2\u00b0F since 1949.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 9 of 12 months. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Bridgeport's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.75 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 44.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1972 (73.93 in); the driest, 1964 (23.03 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 2 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}